      "sourceTextSha256": "e19b846688e036104f5a0845efe357d8a1b8c5e5f018a95d75303a27ebe223a0",
      "text": "Day 10 · Breakfast. City tour (4 hours) with an English-speaking guide, beginning at La Moneda, a historic monument built in neoclassical style in the last years of Spanish rule to house the royal mint and, since the mid-19th century, the seat of the Chilean government. Continue to the Plaza de Armas, where the history of the city began, with the former Governors’ House, the City Hall, the Central Post Office, the Royal Audience building and the Cathedral; climb Santa Lucía Hill for a magnificent panorama, then discover the modern districts of Vitacura, Las Condes and Providencia and drive along the Mapocho River.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1DMIc4Lqk8YLPIAI6ApWDyg-EBSRf3zSe",
