    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "33d79341b7b55b21f67580ee763d9fc3910293d656860f0c7cdb75aaecabf16d",
      "text": "Day 11 · Breakfast. Full-day excursion to Valparaíso, 120 km towards the Pacific, through the Curacaví and Casablanca valleys, known for white wines such as Sauvignon Blanc. Built like an amphitheatre on its hills and linked by historic funiculars, Valparaíso, Chile’s main port, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site: visit Plaza Victoria, Plaza Sotomayor with the Monument to the Heroes of Iquique, and Paseo 21 de Mayo, overlooking the port and the ocean. Continue to Viña del Mar, Chile’s most popular resort, the “Garden City”, for lunch, a walk along the beach and the Quinta Vergara park, home of the International Song Festival. Return to Santiago.",
      "provenance": {
